{
  "description": "Hand-written labelled dataset for CivicFix duplicate detection. Synthetic (written by the developer, not real citizen data). Reports in the same cluster describe the same real-world problem. Offsets are metres east/north; day = days after a fixed base date. Groups are split into dev (used to choose the threshold) and test (used once for the final numbers). A third split, 'stress', was written after the first evaluation to probe cases where location alone fails (different same-category problems very close together; the same problem reported with noisy GPS 100-180 m apart). It is never used for tuning. Because it was designed knowing the distance baseline's weakness, it is deliberately harder for that baseline.",
